{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2101","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Mex in the Grid"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given $$$n^2$$$ cards with values from $$$0$$$ to $$$n^2-1$$$. You are to arrange them in a $$$n$$$ by $$$n$$$ grid such that there is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"exactly"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" one card in each cell."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The MEX (minimum excluded value) of a subgrid$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$ is defined as the smallest non-negative integer that does not appear in the subgrid."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Your task is to arrange the cards such that the sum of MEX values over all $$$\\left(\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}\\right)^2$$$ subgrids is maximized."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$^{\\text{∗}}$$$A subgrid of a $$$n$$$ by $$$n$$$ grid is specified by four numbers $$$l_1, r_1, l_2, r_2$$$ satisfying $$$1\\le l_1\\le r_1\\le n$$$ and $$$1\\le l_2\\le r_2\\le n$$$. The element in the $$$i$$$-th row and the $$$j$$$-th column of the grid is part of the subgrid if and only if $$$l_1\\le i\\le r_1$$$ and $$$l_2\\le j\\le r_2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 100$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1\\le n\\le 500$$$) — the side length of the grid."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$1000$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output $$$n$$$ lines, each containing $$$n$$$ integers representing the elements of the grid. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"If there are multiple answers, you can output any of them."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n2\n3\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0 1 \n2 3 \n8 4 5 \n6 0 1 \n7 2 3"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, one valid arrangement is: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"table_cell"},{"attrs":{"header":false},"children":[{"kind":